[{"text":"ExpandPartialD[exp] expands noncommutative products of QuantumFields and partial differentiation operators in exp and applies the Leibniz rule.","anchor":"expandpartiald"},{"text":"By default the function assumes that there are no expressions outside of exp on which the derivatives inside exp could act. If this is not the case, please set the options LeftPartialD or RIghtPartialD to True.","anchor":"expandpartiald"},{"text":"Overview, ExplicitPartialD, LeftPartialD, LeftRightPartialD, PartialDRelations, RightPartialD, LeftRightNablaD, LeftRightNablaD2, LeftNablaD, RightNablaD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"RightPartialD[\\[Mu]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]]] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\vec{\\partial }_{\\mu }.A_{\\mu }.A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\mu }.\\left(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\nu }\\right)+\\left(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\mu }\\right).A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"RightNablaD[i] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]]] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\vec{\\nabla }^i.A_{\\mu }.A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-A_{\\mu }.\\left(\\partial _iA_{\\nu }\\right)-\\left(\\partial _iA_{\\mu }\\right).A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LeftRightPartialD[\\[Mu]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]]] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overleftrightarrow{\\partial }_{\\mu }.A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\left(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\nu }\\right)-\\overleftarrow{\\partial }_{\\mu }.A_{\\nu }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LeftRightNablaD[i] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]]] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overleftrightarrow{\\nabla }_i.A_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\overleftarrow{\\partial }_i.A_{\\nu }-\\left(\\partial _iA_{\\nu }\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Tau]] RightPartialD[\\[Alpha], \\[Mu], \\[Beta], \\[Nu]] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\tau } \\vec{\\partial }_{\\alpha }.\\vec{\\partial }_{\\mu }.\\vec{\\partial }_{\\beta }.\\vec{\\partial }_{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"CLC[i, j, k] RightNablaD[i, j, k] ExpandPartialD[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{ijk} \\vec{\\nabla }^i.\\vec{\\nabla }^j.\\vec{\\nabla }^k\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"RightPartialD[CartesianIndex[i]] . QuantumField[S, x] % // ExpandPartialD","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\vec{\\partial }_i.S^x\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\partial _iS^x\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"RightPartialD[{CartesianIndex[i], x}] . QuantumField[S, x] % // ExpandPartialD","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\vec{\\partial }_{\\{i,x\\}}.S^x\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\partial _{\\{i,x\\}}S^x\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"By default the derivative won’t act on anything outside of the input expression. But it can be made to by setting the option RightPartialD to True","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ExpandPartialD[RightPartialD[\\[Mu]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]]] . QuantumField[A, LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]]]]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\mu }.\\left(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\nu }\\right)+\\left(\\pa